{"name":"Hacienda Del Sol","hex":"#bb7731","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hacienda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large homestead in a ranch or estate, usually in places where Colonial Spanish culture has had architectural influence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hacienda"},{"term":"del","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Delaware languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The symbol ∇ used to denote the gradient operator.","the symbol ∂, in the context of a partial differential"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/del"},{"term":"sol","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Solos."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In a movable-do or tonic sol-fa system: the fifth step in a scale, preceded by fa and followed by la.\n\nIn a fixed-do system: the musical note G.","In a movable-do or tonic sol-fa system: the fifth step in a scale, preceded by fa and followed by la."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hacienda","blocks":[{"text":"A hacienda is an estate, similar to a Roman latifundium, in Spain and the former Spanish Empire. With origins in Andalusia, haciendas were variously plantations, mines or factories, with many haciendas combining these activities. The word is derived from Spanish hacer and haciendo (making), referring to productive business enterprises."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Hacienda_Lealtad%2C_former_coffee_plantation_in_Lares%2C_Puerto_Rico_03.jpg/330px-Hacienda_Lealtad%2C_former_coffee_plantation_in_Lares%2C_Puerto_Rico_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hacienda","wikidata":"Q917730"},{"title":"Del","blocks":[{"text":"Del, or nabla, is an operator used in mathematics as a vector differential operator, usually represented by ∇. When applied to a function defined on a one-dimensional domain, it denotes the standard derivative of the function as defined in calculus. When applied to a field, it may denote any one of three operations depending on the way it is applied: the gradient or (locally) steepest slope of a scalar field ; the divergence of a vector field; or the curl (rotation) of a vector field."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Del","wikidata":"Q334508"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg/500px-Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg/500px-Hacienda_of_Xcanchakan%281843%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hacienda of Xcanchakan, Yucatán, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHacienda_of_Xcanchakan(1843).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG/500px-Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG/500px-Teatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wheat mill and theatre of Vicente Gallardo; Hacienda Atequiza, Jalisco, Mexico, 1886.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeatro_de_Atequiza%2C_Mexico.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg/500px-Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Hacendado_Propri%C3%A9taire_by_Claudio_Linati_1828.jpg/1280px-Hacend